{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e7381df7683493e4","name":"Blackguard Wilder","source":{"id":"source:reference-e7381df7683493e4","title":"Blackguard Wilder","revision":16254,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:34Z","sha256":"07d5637df534783fc5858ea7d78bf91dde6f85df89ecb4d10f939dc1c39e5ef3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16254","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Blackguard%20Wilder&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e7381df7683493e4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["By slaying a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sher Kar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sher_Kar?action=edit&redlink=1"},", a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blackguard Minion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blackguard_Minion","referenceId":"reference:08f15d2229d4a0c0"}," rises to the rank of Wilder. Dedicated warriors of The Blackguard, these Wilders fall into three specialized ranks to perform their duties: Ravager, Marauder, and Trinity Assassin.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ravagers are the most common Wilders, serving as guards of the Southern Ruins on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mustafar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mustafar","referenceId":"reference:1233775240ba356a"},". They are dedicated defenders of the sanctuary, and the first and last line of defense. Marauders are the most peaceful of the three specialization, traveling away from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mustafar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mustafar","referenceId":"reference:1233775240ba356a"}," to study other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Traditions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Traditions","referenceId":"reference:da4e2621bc8ff060"}," and their lore. This knowledge is used to better ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"},", with new techniques and powers to protect their home. Finally, Trinity Assassins serve the most dangerous of tasks, the elimination of Blackguard enemies. These enemies range in importance from nosy archaeologists, to zealous Jedi Sentinels.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Blackguard Wilder Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," is found almost exclusively on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mustafar"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mustafar","referenceId":"reference:1233775240ba356a"}," in or near the Southern Jedi Ruins, but a few are occasionally located wandering between the ruins and the planet's only remaining city of Fralideja. Blackguard Wilders exist and act more as squad leaders, giving evidence that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"}," might be better organization than most people think possible of a Dark Side cult.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Blackguard Wilder Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://s